On Mon, 1 Dec 2003, Helge Kreutzmann wrote:

> Hello,
> I am currently updating SRM-FAQ. The following questions arose:
>
> a)What is the proper SRM-firmware directory with bootp-support. The
>   current FAQ says
>   ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v5.8/
>   which does not exist; only
>   ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/
>   exists and is empty.

ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v6.6/ is the current
directory, but specifying the current version directory in the faq may not
be a good idea--as soon as a newer version is released the directory
listed in the faq will no longer exist.  Maybe instead just specify
/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/ ?

I may be wrong, but at one point gatekeeper.dec.com and ftp.digital.com
were the same box, but this appears to no longer be the case.

Mike



