On Thursday 11 December 2003 06:44 pm, Jeff DeMaagd wrote:
> Jay Estabrook wrote:
>  > George meant to type that there was no RH 7.3 for Alpha.
>
> Oops!  I don't know where I got the idea that it existed, 7.2 it is.
>
> Michal Jaegermann wrote:
> > On Thu, Dec 11, 2003 at 11:43:21AM -0600, Hoover, Tony wrote:
> >>If you're not opposed to SRM, RedHat 7.x is CD bootable.
> >
> > I booted an installation of 7.2 from CD on UX, i.e. no SRM, using
> > HPWrapper CD and it worked just fine; but if you have SRM available
> > then use it.
>
> I managed to find the ISO.  Is this included with the physical box of RH
> 7.2 Alpha?  I really can't download a 166MB file.

Sorry, but the wrapper came after the physical box sets were created.  The 
HPwrapper was created to wrap about the installation of Red Hat Linux 7.2 for 
Alpha to allow installation of Red Hat Linux 7.2 on Alpha systems which did 
not have kernel support in the original Red Hat 7.2 distribution. It is NOT 
full installation media. Installation with this wrapper requires Red Hat 
Linux 7.2 for Alpha installation media.

Best Regards,


--George



