I've been using bogofilter in my .procmailrc and it seems to be working
fairly well. It's another Bayesian filter that you train by feeding it
examples of spam and non-spam.

After training it with some examples, I just set up my .procmailrc file
like this:

:0HB:
       * ? bogofilter -u -l
       inbox/SPAM/.

This moves spam to an MH style folder where I can review what it has
filtered with sylpheed.Then in sylpheed I have some actions set up to
inform bogofilter about emails it has misclassified. It hasn't caught
everything, but I've gotten no false positives, which is the most
important thing in my mind. 

Allen


